# OneView UI

- Keep **AppShell** / **AuthLayout** structure; do not replace with a new layout system.
- Use design tokens from `index.css` / `theme/tokens.css` and Tailwind maps in `tailwind.config.js` (`brand`, `primary`, `success`, `warning`, `danger`).
- Brand is navy (`#001433` family). Do not introduce purple gradient themes, dark mode, or emoji UI unless asked.
- Permission keys come from `data/navConfig.ts` (`PERMISSION_PAGES`). Guards, menus, and Access Rights must stay aligned.
- Prefer existing shared widgets (report filters, badges, cockpit cards) over one-off duplicates.
- **Single-select dropdowns:** Use `FilterSingleSelect` (toolbar/compact) or `FilterSelect` (forms with empty “Select…” row + `fullWidth`). Same chrome as `FilterMultiSelect` (border button + panel). Trigger layout: label left-truncated, `▾` flush right, equal `px-3` inset on both sides (`inline-flex justify-between gap-3`). Do **not** place the caret immediately after the label text. Do **not** add native HTML `<select>` for new UI. Menu rows are text-only (no radio dots). See `components/FilterSingleSelect.tsx` / `FilterSelect.tsx`.
- **Type-to-search (required):** Every single-select and multi-select menu must include a type-to-search field.
  - **Chrome:** Use shared `DropdownMenuSearch` (`components/DropdownMenuSearch.tsx`) — bordered `h-8` field with inset magnifier, same look as toolbar Resource… search (`rounded-md border border-border … focus:border-accent-line`). Do **not** use a borderless/transparent inline search strip.
  - **Focus on open (required):** When the user opens the dropdown, focus must move to the search input immediately so they can type without an extra click. For portal menus, focus **after** the menu has layout/mounted (e.g. effect on `open && menuLayout`, double `requestAnimationFrame` + `searchRef.focus()`). Escape closes and returns focus to the trigger where applicable.
  - **Keyboard list nav (required):** While focus stays in search: **↓** / **↑** move a highlight through options; **Enter** selects (single-select) or toggles (multi-select; Space also toggles). Highlighted row uses `bg-surface-alt`; scroll into view. Reset highlight when the query changes. Use `utils/dropdownListNav.ts` helpers.
  - Prefer `FilterSingleSelect` / `FilterSelect` / `FilterMultiSelect`. Special-purpose menus (`MinFreeHoursSelect`, Utilization `MonthSelect`, etc.) must use the same `DropdownMenuSearch` chrome + autofocus + keyboard nav behavior.
  - Filter with `matchesSearchQuery`; show “No matches.” when empty.
- **Multi-select filters:** Use `FilterMultiSelect` (same trigger caret layout as single-select; uses `DropdownMenuSearch`).
- **Truncated text:** Any UI using Tailwind `truncate` (ellipsis) must show the full value on hover. App-wide via `TruncateHoverTitles` in `App.tsx`; prefer `TruncateText` for new nodes. See `docs/ui-truncate-tooltips.md`.
- **Toasts:** Use `useToast()` only. Default 5s; hover pauses the timer; dismiss after mouse leave + remaining time. Do not add one-off toasts. See `docs/ui-toast.md`.
- Fonts: Inter (UI) + JetBrains Mono (mono). Do not switch to Inter-only redesigns that drop brand colors.
- Auth screens use `.auth-canvas-bg` / `.auth-canvas-solid`.
- Orphan screens (`ExecutiveDashboard`, `ManagerDashboard`, `Placeholder`) stay unrouted unless explicitly requested.
- **Delete requires confirmation:** Any user-facing delete (soft or hard) must ask for explicit confirmation before executing. Do not delete on a single click without a confirm dialog/step.
